{"type":"text","timestamp":1789787815093,"sessionID":"ses_f4855cf73ffe37M114ntFFYqdE","part":{"id":"prt_0b7aab87c0016Ag67G4xIZM6EZ","messageID":"msg_0b7aaaaff001Nuf2xA95n3PHcU","sessionID":"ses_f4855cf73ffe37M114ntFFYqdE","type":"text","text":"The regression is in the Redis scripts: lock removal and both renewal paths check only whether a lock exists, rather than whether its token matches. Immediate retry also promotes delayed jobs before validating ownership, which can emit events even when the retry is rejected. I’ll restore token checks and move that promotion after validation.\n","time":{"start":1789787814012,"end":1789787815091},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0418e9d80dca9405016aadfea5feb487d19295460aa8a5e7af","phase":"commentary"}}}}
