{"type":"text","timestamp":1789788236671,"sessionID":"ses_f4855cf73ffe37M114ntFFYqdE","part":{"id":"prt_0b7b10ac8001XzaWB08OwolHxv","messageID":"msg_0b7b10550001TRGAlzQ5IOu9jT","sessionID":"ses_f4855cf73ffe37M114ntFFYqdE","type":"text","text":"Fixed the ownership regression in four Redis Lua source files.\n\n- **Job transitions:** Restored token matching in `src/commands/includes/removeLock.lua`. Stale completion, failure, immediate retry, and delayed retry now use the existing lock-mismatch error before changing persisted job data or the replacement owner’s lock.\n- **Lock renewal:** Restored token matching in both `extendLock-2.lua` and `extendLocks-1.lua`, preserving existing failure return values.\n- **Retry events:** Moved delayed-job promotion in `retryJob-11.lua` after ownership validation, preventing rejected retries from changing queue state or emitting promotion events.\n- Preserved missing-lock errors and the intentional `\"0\"` administrative-token behavior.\n\nAdded `tests/worker_ownership.redis.test.ts` with five regression cases covering actual stalled recovery, state/counter/result/event preservation, stale renewal rejection, successful owner renewal and completion, and administrative completion.\n\n**Verification — Node v24.21.0**\n- `npm run build` — passed.\n- Exact requested regression command — **268 tests passed across 7 files**. The initial run hit the shell’s 120-second timeout; rerunning with a longer timeout completed successfully.\n- New regression suite — **5 tests passed**.\n- Targeted ESLint, Prettier, and `git diff --check` — passed.","time":{"start":1789788228296,"end":1789788236669},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_04b36304ef10dfd9016aae00444f6887d1ab2022e03f1a2963","phase":"final_answer"}}}}
